  "prefLabel": "Env-A 104.25 Ozone (O3)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 104.25 “Ozone (O3)” means the most prevalent compound of those compounds called photochemical oxidants, that result from a complex series of atmospheric reactions initiated by being exposed to the ultraviolet component of sunlight.\n\nSource. #1717, eff 2-19-81; ss by #2332, eff 4-29-83; ss by #2938, eff 12-27-84; ss by #5033, eff 12-27-90; ss and moved by #6057-A, eff 6-30-95 (from Env-A 101.67); renumbered by #8256 (from Env-A 101.201), (see Revision Note #1 at chapter heading); renumbered by #8304 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading); renumbered by #9839 (from Env-A 101.136), (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading); ss by #13105, eff 9-25-20 (formerly Env-A 101.138) (see Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Env-A 100)",
